  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Aromatic nucleophilic substitution reaction takes place via the formation of a&nbsp;carbanion intermediate. Hence, the rate of reaction depends on the stability of the carbanion.</p><p>Electron withdrawing effect can stabilise the carbanion. The Electron withdrawing nature of the nitro group will be minimum at the meta position.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Hence the correct answer is</p><p>&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a98a1d7f-2da1-4ed2-870f-4e22e8c18e97-9894252_D.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 205px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
